# (#126) THE PART-2a PARAMETER LEAK, closed for un-named parameters -- and
# the discriminator for the parameter env seed.
#
# Part 2a keys an observed function's numeric parameters into the GLOBAL env
# by name at entry, and there is no env-removal API, so the binding SURVIVED
# the return and a module-scope read of it answered where the VM dies. That
# is #124's known residual, and it was reported as unfixable short of a
# per-call env: "a refusal covering that would reject essentially every
# observed function with a local variable".
#
# Per-name, the seed is emitted only for parameters an observer read NAMES,
# so an un-named parameter is never keyed into the module env and there is
# nothing to leak. Measured, base compiler vs this one:
#
#   VM    moving / Error line 28: undefined variable 'v'  rc 1
#   base  moving / 8                                     rc 0   <- leak
#   new   moving / Error line 28: undefined variable 'v' rc 1
#
# This fixture is also the ONLY thing that discriminates the seed's gate:
# reverting it to the whole-program flag leaves every other observer fixture
# green (measured -- the redundant env write is invisible until something
# reads the leaked name).
define f(v) as:
    local w is v
    w is w * 0.5
    return report of w
print of (f of 8.0)
print of v
